leads", "Expert consensus is Likely R, with two raters at Lean R and one at Tossup", "Prediction markets price Carey near 77%"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Republican district with a well-funded incumbent, but the most recent poll shows Leonard essentially tied, and Democratic outside groups are engaging. That justifies a modest move toward the Democrat from the ratings consensus, landing at a narrow Republican edge with elevated uncertainty.", "watch": "Whether independent or Republican-sponsored polling confirms the tightening seen in the Hart survey, or whether Carey's cash advantage and the R+5 lean reassert themselves.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Carey (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's 15th District leans Republican by about five points, and incumbent Mike Carey returns with a large fundraising edge over Democrat Don Leonard, who has raised a credible but much smaller sum. Most expert raters call the race Likely Republican, though two rate it Lean Republican and one rates it a Tossup.\n\nPolling is thin but notable: a Democratic-sponsored Hart poll from late September shows the race tied at 46-45, a clear shift from earlier summer surveys that had Carey ahead by four to eight points. Prediction markets still price Carey as a strong favorite near 77 percent. The combination of a favorable district, incumbent money, and one recent tightening poll points to a narrow but real Republican advantage with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1732, "margin": -5.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.185, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1905, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1541, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1527, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1532, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1445, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1885, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3